  "name": "Question 1",
  "problem": "Which of the following shaded areas describes the region bounded by the inequality $8x-4y<12?$",
  "worked_solution": "First, we convert the inequality into slope-intercept form:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}8x-4y & <12 \\\\ -4y & <-8x+12 \\\\ 4y & >8x-12 \\\\ y & >2x-3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we proceed as usual. We start by drawing the corresponding straight line $y=2x-3.$ Since the inequality involves a 'strictly greater than' sign, the line $y=2x-3$ itself is *not* part of the solution. Therefore, we draw a dashed line.\n\nThen, we need to decide whether to shade above or below the line. The inequality $y>2x-3$ refers to the $y$-values that are *greater than* those on the line $y=2x-3,$ so we shade *above* the line.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13996642/assets/d399f186d02b777d8b6774833cd9e0855de5f228b1e6872027d7909d2e6dbe6f.png)",
